    <suppress>
        <notes>
            jackson-databind contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor. From 2.8.0 until 2.18.9, 2.21.5, and 3.1.4,
            version 2.22.0 was published on Jun 02, 2026, but still contains the vulnerability. The issue is fixed in 2.22.1, 2.23.0, and 3.2.0.
            version "tools.jackson.core:jackson-core:3.2.0" will implay code changes and may not be compatible with the current code base.
            Therefore, we will suppress this CVE for now.
        </notes>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54515</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54513</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54514</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54512</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2025-21199</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress until="2026-10-31Z">
        <notes>
            CVE-2026-64607 affects Apache HttpComponents Client and is reported against httpclient5 5.6.2. This project already forces
            httpclient5 to 5.6.2, which is currently the latest GA available in Maven Central. Remove this suppression when Apache publishes
            a fixed httpclient5 release.
        </notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.httpcomponents\.client5/httpclient5@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-64607</cve>
    </suppress>
